## Source audit follow-up

The ProcessQueue and PopProcessQueue timeout caches were already separate for
their direct expiry methods, but Push rebalance had used the ProcessQueue value
for both assignment types. It now carries separate timeout slots and uses the
PopProcessQueue value when evaluating POP assignments. Constructing a POP
queue initializes its class-equivalent property cache. The regression
`broker_assignment_error_preserves_worker_until_empty_assignment` sets a very
large ProcessQueue timeout and an expired POP timeout, then checks that the POP
assignment is replaced. The cache lifetime check is
`pop_process_queue_pull_idle_property_keeps_its_first_java_class_value`.

